00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.980
At any rate, for as much as I loved "It",

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.700
y'all know that I couldn't go see it without getting the old "Theorist Gears" a-greased!

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.800
And I had a thought towards the end of the movie--

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.460
How are these kids able to survive all of Pennywise's attacks?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.040
Pennywise successfully targets other children, like Georgie and Betty Ripson, (Rest In Pepperoni)

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.600
but even when alone with individual members of the Losers Club, Pennywise can't make the kill.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.970
I mean, obviously as main characters, the easy explanation here is that they all have plot armor!

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:28.120
But after doing my homework into "It" and the rest of Stephen King's work, I found my answer...

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.800
The Losers Club isn't just a group of ordinary kids, all of these kids SHINE.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.100
*OH YEAH MY THAT'S MY JAM* (lmao, agreed)

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.320
No, not like a giant supernatural crab-- though, come to think of it,

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.060
that's more of Pennywise's domain...and oh boy, for those of you

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.420
who don't know how the rest of It goes, you are in for a WEIRD ride!

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.620
No, what I mean to say is these kids shine like

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.420
Danny Torrance from another Stephen King work

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.760
you've probably heard of: The Shining.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.100
If it's been a minute since you saw that movie, let me help you out.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.960
Shining means having some level of psychic ability.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:03:02.480
In The Shining, Danny's shine gives him the ability to communicate with others telepathically and interact with supernatural beings.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.480
He's basically Bran from Game of Thrones, but with more emotions and more working legs. (ding! ding!)

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.100
And when you look at the evidence, it's pretty clear that the Losers Club also has this psychic shine ability.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.000
So, in today's episode, I'm gonna break it down for you like a crazy man with an axe!

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.880
Heeeeere's MAT PAT!

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.660
Now some people might think this theory is over before it even begins

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:26.100
Since nobody in It references psychic powers, the Overlook Hotel, or the fact that the moon landing didn't happen.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.000
You know, all those things that are normally associated with the Shining.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.299
But here's the thing--

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:35.839
Stephen King puts Marvel and Pixar to SHAME with how interconnected his universe is! He was doing a dark

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:43.279
connected universe before the Dark Connected Universe began! And also apparently after it ended, too...Here are just a few ways It connects to the

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.769
wider Stephen King-averse. The Losers Club is mentioned

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:50.320
by name in his novel, "Dreamcatcher" Mike Hanlon, one of the club's members grows up to be the town's

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:57.620
librarian in Derry, which we see in another King novel, "Insomnia," and somebody even sees glowing clown eyes in a storm drain in the "Tommyknockers."

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.160
But we're not just talking about a general shared universe here--

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:07.240
It has direct connections to the shining through one man-- Dick Hallorann. Chef of the Overlook Hotel.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:12.420
In a scene in It, Chapter One, Ben recaps some of the past tragedies that have happened in Derry.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.280
One of them is a fire that happened at the "Black Spot",

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:20.680
an African-American nightclub that burned down during a past visit from Pennywise in 1962. (why do ppl like him so much)

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.520
One of the people who survived that fire: Dick Hallorann.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:29.200
In fact, Dick actually saves Mike Hanlan's father from DYING in that fire!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.680
And here's the best part-- Dick possesses the Shine himself.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.740
In fact, throughout the Shining, he teaches Danny about the gift and communicates telepathically with him!

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:40.720
How'd you like some ice cream, doc? (he'd make a great grandpa, y'know.)

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.119
So having a character with psychic abilities serve as the bridge between the two stories

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.910
not only shows us that we're working in the same universe,

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:53.960
but also that the ability to shine is definitely something that exists in the world of It.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.320
So what kind of indication do we have that the kids in the Losers Club ACTUALLY shine?

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.480
We don't actually see too much of it in this first movie,

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:06.540
but you will DEFINITELY start to see it crop up in It, Chapter 2, because the clues are definitely there in the novel.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.760
You see, in the story of It, all the kids grow up to be unusually successful,

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.900
but they all have to return to Derry to once again face Pennywise and finish him off for good.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:19.520
Bill as an adult fights It through a psychic battle of wills known as the "ritual of Chud."

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.980
Now, this is gonna sound really weird if you haven't read the book--

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.260
actually, scratch that, it's pretty weird even if you HAVE read the book,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.600
but Bill is instructed by an interdimensional turtle, yeah, a, a turtle, (wh)

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:33.960
that the only way to defeat It for GOOD is to engage in this ritual and use his imagination

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.700
as a psychic counterbalance to It's powers.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.520
The battle is done entirely telepathically.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.520
Now look at the description that Dick Hallorann uses when he's describing what the shine is!

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:58.580
At this point, some of you still might not believe-- which is dangerous, because belief is what keeps Pennywise from eating you. :^) Nonetheless, you might be thinking that

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:03.660
this theory has a few holes in it-- kinda like Dick Hallorann at the end of the Shining! (NO!!!!!) BaDOOM ching!

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:09.119
Let's try to plug those holes in with more evidence, shall we? Towards the end of the novel It, Mike Hanlon is in the hospital,

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.730
far away from the rest of the Losers Club who're descending into Its lair. You would think Mike would be safe,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:19.830
but in actuality, there's someone in his room waiting to kill him. Bill, again from deep in the sewers,

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.200
suddenly senses that Mike is in trouble and instructs the group to quote,

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:32.180
at which point the club locks hands and sends Mike psychic energy to fight off his attacker like a Goku-sized          spirit Bomb.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:38.860
And it's not just Bill! The novel clearly states that Bev feels something LEAVE them and go to Mike! Quote from

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.200
-- yeah, in case you didn't know, It is a LOOONG book!

00:06:54.669 --> 00:06:55.169
End quote.

00:06:55.169 --> 00:06:56.100
And then a few sentences later,

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:21.420
So again, we're seeing references to these kids having a quote-unquote, "second sight" and feeling psychic power.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:28.100
transitioning BETWEEN them, and during the ritual of Chud, Bill isn't the only one telepathically communicating with It, Ben

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.420
actually begins the battle by reading Its mind! Quote,

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:41.220
End quote.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:47.399
So that's Bill, Bev, Mike, and now Ben, all with some sort of reference to telepathy or psychic ability.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:53.429
We can even include RICHIE in this because he ALSO engages in the telepathic ritual of Chud, and communicates with Bill

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.729
psychically during that moment of the novel. We even see that Ritchie actually shares a psychic connection with other members of the town,

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.580
specifically an Irish police officer named "Nell."

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:10.080
It's not important for us to go into, just know that it happens. Anyway, VERY long and VERY complicated story short, the psychic

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:15.210
connection is shared between all of the members of the losers Club. Its strongest with Bill,

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:22.739
but all the others have instances where they feel or sense something telepathically, which begs the question. Why. Why these kids?

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:28.169
What's the probability of having so many shiners in the same town, let alone the same group? Well...

00:08:28.169 --> 00:08:31.889
there's actually a pretty clear explanation. The shine tends to

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:36.088
show up in kids were victims of abuse. In the Shining, Jack Torrance,

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:39.899
Danny's father, was a violent alcoholic. 
We hear in the movie and

00:08:40.329 --> 00:08:45.689
repeatedly in the novel that he dislocated Danny's arm during one of his drunken rages, and his wife Wendy's

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:51.149
description of it as just an accident certainly makes it sound like there's either a lot more there...or that it's happened before.

00:08:51.149 --> 00:08:52.700
...And then he had a injury.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.100
What sort of injury did he have?

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.180
My husband had been..been drinking,

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:04.380
and...he came home about three hours late, so he wasn't exactly in the greatest mood that night...

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:09.980
...on, this particular occasion, my husband just.. used too much

00:09:09.989 --> 00:09:13.000
strength, and he injured Danny's arm.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.900
I guess that's about the time when I first noticed that he(, danny btw,) was talking to Tony.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.769
Also notice that Danny's psychic ability, which he's nicknamed Tony,

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:20.519
it's weird,

00:09:20.519 --> 00:09:28.109
but don't get confused there...Tony doesn't appear until after this traumatic accident at the hands of his dad. In the Shining sequel, Doctor

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.360
Sleep, yeah, there's a sequel...

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:33.897
Today's episode is just full of surprises...We find out that when Dick Hallorann was a child, he was

00:09:33.897 --> 00:09:39.360
sexually and physically abused by his grandfather. It doesn't seem like a coincidence that two characters

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.529
who are confirmed to have the Shine were both victims of childhood violence. Now,

00:09:43.529 --> 00:09:48.779
let's go through the Losers Club. Bill is bullied for his stutter, Bev is sexually abused by her creepy father,

00:09:48.939 --> 00:09:53.039
Richie's abuse isn't explicit in the movie, but he actually suffers from parental neglect

00:09:53.079 --> 00:09:56.579
which is the reason why he feels the need to constantly keep talking and be funny,

00:09:56.579 --> 00:10:01.529
he doesn't want people to abandon him. Eddie is the victim of his mother's Munchausen Syndrome by proxy,

00:10:01.839 --> 00:10:03.519
being diagnosed with fake

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:09.448
ailments to make him think he's sick so that she can control his life. Mike is called an outsider in the most recent movie,

00:10:09.449 --> 00:10:15.389
but the old miniseries and novel make it pretty clear that Mike is the victim of racial slurs and racially motivated violence.

00:10:15.639 --> 00:10:18.539
Stan is bullied for being Jewish, and Ben is bullied for being

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:24.209
overweight in the original movie and for being the new kid in the reboot. Given the fact that all these people share a history of

00:10:24.209 --> 00:10:29.698
trauma and exhibit some level of telekinetic ability, isn't it possible that shining is developed as a coping mechanism?

00:10:29.889 --> 00:10:33.779
So there you have it! A shining theory not rooted in moon-landing conspiracies.

00:10:33.779 --> 00:10:39.029
But so what? Even if the kids in It are like Dick and Danny and the Shining, does any of that really matter?

00:10:39.029 --> 00:10:41.029
Well, yeah, actually it does,

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:47.760
ABSOLUTELY it does! It might not just be that the kids have the same power, it might also mean that they're fighting the same EVIL.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:52.680
Considering that It is a shapeshifter, and is really just a manifestation of evil energy from the multiverse,

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:57.629
why couldn't It be the evil at the Overlook Hotel? A deeper look into this is probably a theory for another day,

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:01.800
but let's just do some quick detective work to talk about how the evil operates in both the Shining

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.859
and It. Towards the end of the Shining, Jack, crazy and completely

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:10.410
consumed by the spirits of the Overlook Hotel, is locked in the pantry by his wife Wendy. Near the end of It,

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:12.190
We catch up with adult Henry Bowers

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:18.869
who's gone completely crazy and is locked in a mental asylum. In both instances, a ghost appears to the men. For Jack

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:24.750
it's Delbert Grady-- the former caretaker of the hotel who killed his family and wants Jack to do the same. For Henry Bowers,

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:31.319
it's his old henchman Belch who wants Henry to go kill the Losers Club. Both Jack in the Shining and Henry in It are imprisoned,

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.440
but their respective

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:38.279
ghostly visions say that they can get him out in exchange for the respective men committing murder. And we know in both of these instances

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.640
that they aren't

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.020
hallucinations because in both

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:48.120
situations, the ghosts provide them with a physical murder weapon. The croquet mallet for Jack, and the switchblade for Henry.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:51.539
It's the exact same tactic with the exact same goal.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.720
Maybe it's not so much that

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:59.910
Pennywise can't kill people who shine but rather just knows how dangerous people who shine can be because they can use the ritual of chud

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:06.149
By employing Jack Torrance to kill his son Danny and Henry Bowers to kill the losers Club the threat to it is

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:11.010
Effectively wiped out and it can continue to terrorize and feast on others who are less psychically

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:16.499
Inclined and when you consider that all these Stephen King's stories share a universe does it have to stop there

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:23.579
I couldn't evil energy that creates Pennywise possess a dog like in Cujo or create a bunch of pet zombies like in Pet Sematary

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:28.080
Or convince a girl to murder her classmates in Carrie if Pennywise is a shapeshifter

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:32.490
That opens the door for it to be the evil in pretty much every Stephen King story

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:38.759
Ever a clown a hotel an evil car or anything else it might even mean that Pennywise doesn't go into hibernation

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:43.319
